<article class="env-lemma" id="0ABX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ABX">Lemma <span data-tag="0ABX">68.17.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. If $X$ is decent (resp. is reasonable, resp. has property $(\beta )$ of Lemma <a href="/tag/03JX" data-tag="03JX">68.5.1</a>), then $f$ is decent (resp. reasonable, resp. has property $(\beta )$). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $T$ be a scheme and let $T \to Y$ be a morphism. Then $T \to Y$ is representable, hence the base change $T \times _ Y X \to X$ is representable. Hence if $X$ is decent (or reasonable), then so is $T \times _ Y X$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0ABT" data-tag="0ABT">68.6.5</a>. Similarly, for property $(\beta )$, see Lemma <a href="/tag/03KF" data-tag="03KF">68.5.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>